  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "State vs Shamim on 7 May, 2025 In The Court Of Ms. Aayushi Saxena, Judicial Magistrate First Class-05, Shahdara District, Karkardooma Courts, Delhi Cr Case No. -: 4501/2018 Cnr No. -: Dlsh020067232018 Fir No. -: 167/2017",
    "facts": "Briefly stated, the case of the prosecution is that on 13.06.2017 at 11:30 PM under the Karkarimor Flyover Red Light, Delhi, accused Shamim was found driving a truck, bearing registration number UP-12L-5166, in a rash and negligent manner so as to endanger human life and safety of others and while driving so, accused struck against a Wagon R car, which was driven by a person namely Sukhbir Singh (deceased), as a result of which the said person namely Sukhbir Singh died. On the basis of the complaint, FIR was registered under Section 279/304Aof the Indian Penal Code, 1860 (hereinafter, \"IPC\"). INVESTIGATION AND APPEARANCE OF ACCUSED- 2. After registration of the FIR, the Investigating Officer (hereinafter, \"IO\") undertook investigation and on culmination of the investigation, the Police Report under Section 173 Cr.P.C., against the accused persons was filed. 3. Vide order dated 02.08.2018, Ld. Predecessor of this Court took cognizance of the offence and issued summons to the accused. 4. Thereafter, on appearance of accused, copy of charge-sheet alongwith documents annexed therewith were supplied to him as FIR No. 167/2017 PS Jagatpuri State Vs. Shamim Page no. 2 of 7 per section 207 Cr.P.C. 5. On 02.04.2019, on finding a prima facie case against accused Shamim, notice under Section 279/304A IPC was framed against him by Ld. Predecessor of this Court, to which he pleaded not guilty and claimed trial. Dead body identification, which were Ex.P12 & Ex.P13. Accordingly, witnesses at serial no. 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14 and 19 were dropped as admitted from the list of witnesses. He further deposed that one Wagon R car was in-front of his car and when he reached near fly over from Karkardooma towards Parparganj/flyover from Jagatpuri to Patparganj, he took the road below the flyover and one tempo/truck crossed his car from the left side and came in front of his car and the truck driver applied breaks as it was red light, due to which the above-said Wagon R car got hit with the tempo from behind. He further deposed that he also applied the breaks and the person inside the Wagon R car got stuck and some public persons along with beggars stopped and with their help, the Wagon R car driver was taken out of the car. He further deposed that he gave water to the person driving Wagon R from his car and he made a PCR call. He further deposed that he inquired from the said injured person, regarding his condition, to which he stated that he was fine and PW-1 made the call to wife of the injured from the mobile phone of the injured and informed about the accident and they came within 5-10 minutes. He further deposed that the injured refused to go to the hospital when requested by police officials. He further deposed that his statement was not recorded on that day but later his statement was recorded. He further deposed that he could not tell the number of the truck or the wagon R car and he could not identify by face the driver of the truck though he was one Muslim person wearing a cap. He further deposed that he saw that the injured in wagon R car looked tired and sleepy. At that stage witness was shown the photographs on the judicial file, seeing which witness stated them to be the photographs of the car of the uncle and the same were FIR No. 167/2017 PS Jagatpuri State Vs. Shamim Page no. 4 of 7 exhibited as Ex. A1, A2, A3, A4 and A5. At that stage, witness was shown the photographs on the judicial file seeing which witness stated them to be the photographs of a truck and the same were exhibited as Ex.A6 to A11 and stated that he could not say whether the same were of offending truck or not. At that stage, Ld. APP for the State sought permission to cross examine the witness as he was not supporting the case of prosecution and has turned hostile. During cross examination of PW-1 by Ld. APP for the State, he deposed that \" I can not say with surety whether the date of incident is 13.06.2017. Summons and BWs were repeatedly issued to PW Kapil Bansal (cited as an eye witness) but the same were received back unexecuted.",
    "arguments": "11. It has been held in case of Sadhu Singh V/s State of Punjab 1997(3) Crime 55 the Hon'ble Punjab & Haryana High Court :- \"In a criminal trial, it is for the prosecution to establish its case beyond all reasonable doubts. If the prosecution appears to be improbable or lacks credibility the benefit of doubt necessarily has to go to the accused.\" FIR No. 167/2017 PS Jagatpuri State Vs. Shamim Page no. 6 of 7 DECISION 12.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "11. It has been held in case of Sadhu Singh V/s State of Punjab 1997(3) Crime 55 the Hon'ble Punjab & Haryana High Court :- \"In a criminal trial, it is for the prosecution to establish its case beyond all reasonable doubts. If the prosecution appears to be improbable or lacks credibility the benefit of doubt necessarily has to go to the accused.\" FIR No. 167/2017 PS Jagatpuri State Vs. Shamim Page no. 6 of 7 DECISION 12."
  },
